lifornia is just this land of Eden ISM  and horribleness you know despite the  fact that they actually have a pretty  pretty decent economy out there they're  moving forward on renewable energy but  yeah don't do that  Texas apparently because that means  bringing in tofu and dyed hair is what  Cruz warned people about I'm gonna bring  dyed hair to the state of Texas because  apparently based on Cruz's statement up  till this point  you couldn't dye your hair in Texas  there was no hair dye Peto a wark  is the guy who's gonna bring in the hair  dye for the state of Texas according to  Ted Cruz Cruz has gone after him for  being a former member of a punk rock  band as if that's something to be  ashamed of you know you really want to  resonate with the younger voters go  after music that's a smart idea saying  look how awesome this guy was he was in  a band  ooh right yeah probably not gonna work  out so well at the polls with the  younger crowd nonetheless it's what Ted  Cruz has done but I think personally the  most disgusting thing that Ted Cruz is  done during his race against Beto award  is begging Donald Trump to come to Texas  to hold a rally to help save him the  reason that's so disgusting one we've  seen the Trump rallies they're not about  the candidate at all they're about him  and Texas is probably a place that's  gonna play pretty well you sit there  brag about yourself for an hour  everybody loves it you talk about how  you hate those people coming across the  border they love it but let's not forget  what Donald Trump did to Ted Cruz during  the presidential campaign I  Donald Trump not only insulted Ted Cruz  personally he insulted his wife's  appearance and he also gave credence to  the conspiracy theory that had Cruz's  father was involved in the JFK  assassination Donald Donald Trump helped  kind of push that and now Ted Cruz in  spite of the fact that the man has  insulted every branch of his family tree  still says please come and help me and  save me from Beto  if I were living in the state of Texas  and I was an independent voter and I saw  that and I saw that this man valued that  Senate seat more than he values his own  wife his father any member of his family  that would immediately be disqualifying  for me I wouldn't tolerate it I wouldn't  accept it I wouldn't condone it and I  sure as heck wouldn't vote for it and I  think that's what the voters in the  state of Texas need to understand  sometimes you go past the policy  sometimes you do look at just the  personal character of someone and if Ted  Cruz values that little Senate seat so  much more than he values his own wife  to ask the man who attacked her to come  and campaign for him then yeah that  should be disqualifying another attack  that Cruz is levied on Beto and I love  talking about this because Cruz is such  a disgusting character is the fact that  he's mocking federal war for going by  Beto instead of Robert because according  to Cruz he's just trying to appeal to  the Latino community  Hispanics immigrants by changed his name  to Beto  really Rafael that's where you want to  be you want to be talking about people  changing their name mr. Rafael Cruz I  don't think that's exactly where you  should be going with your line of  attacks Ted Cruz is in trouble he knows  he's in trouble but more importantly  other Republicans in the country know  that he's in trouble last week Mick  Mulvaney from the cfpv gave a speech  New York where he said Ted Cruz is  likely going to lose in Texas but it's  okay because we're probably gonna pick  up that Senate seat down in Florida with  Rick Scott running against Bill Nelson  but he said Cruz is probably gonna lose  because he's so the bull now mo vanie  actually said this to a group of  Republican donors gathered in New York  that Cruz is so unlikable and he's right  we actually know that from the time that  Ted Cruz worked on george w bush's 2000  campaign because he wasn't offered a job  within the administration after the  victory because nobody there liked him  when everyone that's ever spent time  with the man comes forward and says wow  i really dislike him maybe that should  tell the voters something you only know  the man from afar you only see him on TV  you see him at a campaign spot you don't  have to deal with him one-on-one but  just take the word of the people who  have had to do that even those who agree  with him on everything they still say  that he is an unlikable creep which  probably should give you enough to know  when you go to the polls and cast your  ballot you want to vote for the guy who  actually wants to do something about the  state of Texas better or Roarke wants to  make things better or do you want to  vote for the guy that even his closest  friends say is just really really  unlikable

